# Scope Control

Agents MUST NOT independently:

- Change service boundaries or move domain logic between services
- Replace PostgreSQL or introduce another primary database
- Replace API Gateway or change authentication architecture
- Change tenant architecture or trust-boundary model
- Replace the Go backend stack or Vue/Nuxt frontend stack
- Introduce Kafka, RabbitMQ, or similar messaging unless explicitly authorized
- Rename broad public APIs or remove existing services
- Perform repository-wide refactors or mass formatting
- Change deployment architecture or run destructive cleanup (`docker volume prune`, database wipe)
- Modify generated files without need

Such changes require an explicit architecture task or ADR.

Allowed routine work stays within assigned paths and frozen contracts defined in the agent task template.
